      "title": "China says it doesn’t recognise U.T. of Ladakh; spars with India over naming geographical features",
      "link": "https://www.thehindu.com/news/national/mea-reaffirms-ladakh-is-an-integral-part-of-india-says-chinas-denial-cannot-change-facts/article71579210.ece",
      "description": "Spat comes 10 days after the Survey of India announced the standardisation of the names of specific relief features in Ladakh, including 11 peaks, five mountains, six land areas, two glaciers, two passes, one valley, one river, one lake, and one other water body",
      "source_name": "The Hindu National",
      "published": "2026-10-13T17:25:39"
    },
    {
      "title": "India rejects China's objection to standard names for 28 Ladakh places",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/india-rejects-china-s-objection-to-standard-names-for-28-ladakh-places-126101301028_1.html",
      "description": "India on Tuesday rejected Beijing's objection to New Delhi announcing standard names of 28 places and features in Ladakh, asserting that the Union territory is an \"integral and inalienable\" part of the country.\nLast week, the Union home ministry assigned the standard names to the places and geographical features in Ladakh, including certain key border friction points along the Line of Actual Control (LAC) such as Gogra and Hot Spring.\nIndia's reaction came hours after China strongly opposed New Delhi assigning the standardised names.\n\"It is reiterated that the UT (Union Territory) of Ladakh is an integral and inalienable part of India. No amount of denial by the Chinese side can change this established fact,\" External Affairs Ministry spokesperson Randhir Jaiswal said.\nHe said the press release by the Ministry of Home Affairs dated October 2 that China referred to, is \"self-explanatory\".\n\"The announcement mentions that the 28 places/features located in the UT of Ladakh have been .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-13T18:02:00"
    },
    {
      "title": "China opposes India's move to name 28 strategic locations in Ladakh",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/external-affairs-defence-security/news/china-opposes-india-s-move-to-name-28-strategic-locations-in-ladakh-126101300612_1.html",
      "description": "China on Tuesday strongly opposed India's decision to assign standardised names to 28 strategic locations and geographical features in Ladakh, claiming that the areas belonged to it.\n\"China has never recognised the so-called 'Union Territory of Ladakh' unilaterally and illegally established by India,\" Foreign Ministry spokesperson Mao Ning told a media briefing here.\nBeijing, she said, \"firmly opposes India's announcement of so-called standard names\".\nMao was responding to a question on India's Ministry of Home Affairs announcing standardised names for 28 places and geographical features in Ladakh.\n\"The move is illegal and invalid and cannot change the fact that the relevant areas in the western sector of the China-India boundary have always belonged to China,\" she said.\nOn October 2, India formally identified 28 strategic locations and geographical features in Ladakh, including key border friction points along the Line of Actual Control (LAC) such as Gogra and Hot Spring, on the",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-13T09:09:28"
    }
